  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#adoption-agency-algorithm\r\n\r\nWhat exactly does this text mean:\r\n> If there is no such element, then return and instead act as described in the \"any other end tag\" entry above.\r\n\r\nWhat UA should do after executing steps in \"any other end tag\"?\r\n1. Should a call site look like this:\r\n```cpp\r\nif (adoption_agency(token) == run_any_other_end_tag)\r\n    goto any_other_end_tag;\r\n// further steps will NOT be executed\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. Or like this:\r\n```cpp\r\nif (adoption_agency(token) == run_any_other_end_tag)\r\n    any_other_end_tag(token);\r\n// further steps will be executed\r\n```\r\n\r\n[Ladybird behaves like 1][1], [Chrome] and [html5lib] - like 2 (they call `any_other_end_tag` directly from `adoption_agency`). [Firefox], [gumbo], and [lexbor] don't call `any_other_end_tag` at all (they ignore the return value of `adoption_agency`).\r\n\r\n[1]: https://github.com/SerenityOS/serenity/blob/96d5a1edb0/Userland/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/Parser/HTMLParser.cpp#L1897\r\n[gumbo]: https://github.com/google/gumbo-parser/blob/a0f9059087c/src/parser.c#L2706\r\n[lexbor]: https://github.com/lexbor/lexbor/blob/179309054c/source/lexbor/html/tree/insertion_mode/in_body.c#L930\r\n[Chrome]: https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/b0dfea838c/third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/parser/html_tree_builder.cc#L1701\r\n[Firefox]: https://github.com/mozilla/gecko-dev/blob/00e6644d0db8acf/parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilder.cpp#L1260\r\n[html5lib]: https://github.com/html5lib/html5lib-python/blob/3e500bb6e4188/html5lib/html5parser.py#L1437",
